  "notes": [
    "VCC is pin 4 and GND is pin 11, in the middle of each side rather than at the corners. Most quad op-amps (TL074, MCP6004) use the same pins. It is the 74xx logic chips that put power at 14 and 7, which is why this one catches people out.",
    "Same amplifier as the LM358: single supply, output reaches near ground but stops about 1.5 V below V+, 1 MHz gain bandwidth, crossover distortion in the output stage.",
    "Not rail to rail. On a 3.3 V rail you have almost no usable output swing, which is why modern designs reach for an MCP6004 instead.",
    "The LM339 is the comparator in this package and is NOT pin compatible with the LM324. Its supply pins are 3 and 12, and its outputs are open collector.",
    "Unused amplifiers should be wired as unity-gain followers with the input tied to a mid-rail reference, not left floating."
  ],
